              "type": "text",
              "content": "Science and Society"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.775,
            0.866,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cyberbullying",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " involves the use of digital devices such as phones, computers, or online platforms to harass others by sending misleading messages, spreading false rumours, or sharing personal information without consent (Fig. 6.4). However, if someone tries to bully you, it is important not to feel scared or helpless. Rather, handle it wisely and seek help from parents and teachers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.876,
            0.866,
            0.913
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Additionally, you should be cautious when uploading any picture online or sharing personal information with strangers."
            }
          ]
        },
